1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,498
My name is Mitch.

2
00:00:01,518 --> 00:00:04,248
I want to tell you about the thing that
visited

3
00:00:04,268 --> 00:00:06,947
me after I moved into my brother's house.

4
00:00:06,967 --> 00:00:09,179
I used to call ghosts nonsense.

5
00:00:09,199 --> 00:00:12,211
Then something climbed through my window
with empty

6
00:00:12,231 --> 00:00:15,456
black eyes, and I stopped laughing at
nonsense.

7
00:00:15,476 --> 00:00:17,155
Let us go back to the beginning.

8
00:00:17,755 --> 00:00:22,827
A week after my own house was foreclosed,
I moved in with my brother Edwin.

9
00:00:22,847 --> 00:00:26,696
We had not spoken in ten years, so I was
glad to be there,

10
00:00:26,716 --> 00:00:30,451
and that first night I fell asleep fast,
happy for once.

11
00:00:31,051 --> 00:00:35,096
Around one in the morning I heard rustling
outside my window.

12
00:00:35,116 --> 00:00:39,210
I told myself it was only a raccoon and
went back to sleep.

13
00:00:39,230 --> 00:00:43,727
In the morning I mentioned it to Edwin,
and he agreed it was probably nothing.

14
00:00:44,327 --> 00:00:48,575
The next night I woke to the sound of my
window sliding open, then

15
00:00:48,595 --> 00:00:52,949
a heavy thump on the floor, as if
something had climbed inside.

16
00:00:52,969 --> 00:00:56,364
I sat up and searched the room, but I saw
nothing there.

17
00:00:56,384 --> 00:00:58,258
"You look terrible this morning, Mitch."

18
00:00:58,858 --> 00:01:02,656
Edwin dropped his coffee cup the moment he
saw my face.

19
00:01:02,676 --> 00:01:04,590
He held up a mirror for me.

20
00:01:04,610 --> 00:01:07,917
A long gash had opened across my left
cheek overnight,

21
00:01:07,937 --> 00:01:10,401
and I had no memory of how it got there.

22
00:01:11,001 --> 00:01:14,315
At the hospital the doctor lifted my shirt
to show me a

23
00:01:14,335 --> 00:01:17,827
fresh, sewn incision where a kidney should
have been.

24
00:01:17,847 --> 00:01:20,221
"You somehow lost your left kidney last
night.

25
00:01:20,241 --> 00:01:22,551
We do not know how. I am sorry, Mitch."

26
00:01:22,571 --> 00:01:23,912
I could not answer him.

27
00:01:24,512 --> 00:01:29,171
On the third night I woke at midnight to a
creature leaning over my bed,

28
00:01:29,191 --> 00:01:34,150
a dark hoodie pulled low, a cracked blue
mask with no mouth and no nose.

29
00:01:34,170 --> 00:01:37,235
Where its eyes should have been there was
only black,

30
00:01:37,255 --> 00:01:40,340
empty sockets, with a black fluid dripping
from them.

31
00:01:40,940 --> 00:01:45,746
It lunged for my chest with long pale
fingers, clawing for my ribs.

32
00:01:45,766 --> 00:01:49,189
I grabbed the camera from the mantel and
took one picture

33
00:01:49,209 --> 00:01:52,147
before I kicked it hard in the face and
ran.

34
00:01:52,167 --> 00:01:55,714
I grabbed my wallet and fled into the dark
woods behind the

35
00:01:55,733 --> 00:01:59,300
house, until I tripped on a rock and
everything went black.

36
00:01:59,900 --> 00:02:04,276
I woke again in a hospital bed with only
minor injuries.

37
00:02:04,296 --> 00:02:09,371
The doctor said my parents were coming to
collect me, and then his face changed.

38
00:02:09,391 --> 00:02:12,223
"Your brother has been killed by some...
thing. I am sorry."

39
00:02:12,823 --> 00:02:16,301
My parents drove me back to gather my
remaining things.

40
00:02:16,321 --> 00:02:20,408
In the hallway lay Edwin's body, and
beside it something small.

41
00:02:20,428 --> 00:02:24,030
I picked it up without telling my parents
what I had found,

42
00:02:24,050 --> 00:02:28,102
and in the car I finally looked down at
what I was holding.

43
00:02:28,122 --> 00:02:31,703
This story is inspired by the Eyeless Jack
creepypasta,

44
00:02:31,723 --> 00:02:35,361
first written and shared online in twenty
twelve.

45
00:02:35,381 --> 00:02:36,616
Now tell me.

46
00:02:36,636 --> 00:02:38,910
Would you have believed it was only a
raccoon?

